From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:10:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: inline small functions in the 68k template
 JIT

- op_call and op_call_ignore_result: at a site whose call link holds
  a JavaScript callee, a function of at most 64 bytecode bytes
  (m68kTemplateJITMaximumInlineSize) whose instructions all have fast
  code is written into the caller's code. A guard word checks the call
  link still holds that CodeBlock; it is cleared when the CodeBlock
  dies (reconcileCaches). The callee runs on the frame a call would
  give it, with the prologue's stack check; op_ret copies the result
  and moves cfr back.
- Anything the fast code does not take goes to a bail stub that
  finishes the frame (caller frame, return point, metadataTable,
  CodeBlock, call site) and redispatches at that instruction, which
  then returns to the call's return point.
- An inlined function may call: the frame is finished first, and sp
  and PB are put back at its return. A function that calls nothing is
  also inlined into an inlined one.
- op_to_this: fast code for a final object with the cached structure.
- useM68KInlining (on) turns it off.

Team 3
---
 .../JavaScriptCore/llint/M68KTemplateJIT.cpp  | 266 +++++++++++++++++-
